@startuml
!pragma teoz true
hide footbox
skinparam defaultFontName Microsoft YaHei
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ParticipantPadding 24
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 100
title SIM-ddd-sequence — source snapshot (not a runtime trace)
participant "obj: 调用者" as obj
participant "ctl: AuthorizationController" as ctl
participant "rest: RestSupport" as rest
participant "directory: DirectoryApplicationService" as directory
participant "auth: AuthorizationApplicationService" as auth
participant "repo: AuthorizationRepository" as repo
participant "«MetaClass»\n: RestSupport" as restType
activate obj
obj -> ctl: 1. check(bearer, input) or explain(bearer, input)
activate ctl
note over ctl
/authorization/check passes explain=false.
/authorization/explain passes explain=true.
end note
ctl -> ctl: 2. check(bearer, input, explain)
activate ctl
ctl -> rest: 3. principal(bearer)
activate rest
rest -->> ctl: principal
deactivate rest
ctl -> auth: 4. require(principal, rbac:authz:invoke, false)
activate auth
auth -->> ctl: actor
deactivate auth
break identifier does not match UI / API kind
ctl -->> obj: 400 INVALID_AUTHORIZATION_REQUEST
end
note over ctl
Use the requested userId, or actor.id() if omitted.
end note
opt target differs from actor
ctl -> directory: 5. user(principal, targetUserId)
activate directory
directory -->> ctl: target within department scope
deactivate directory
end
ctl -> auth: 6. simulate(targetUserId, system, kind, identifier)
activate auth
auth -> auth: 7. stableSimulation(targetUserId, system, kind, identifier)
activate auth
loop until terminal result, at most 3 attempts
auth -> repo: 8. version()
activate repo
repo -->> auth: initial version
deactivate repo
group Target status and decision
auth -> auth: 9. unavailableReason(targetUserId, system)
activate auth
auth -> repo: 10. systemEnabled(system)
activate repo
repo -->> auth: enabled
deactivate repo
auth -> repo: 11. identity(targetUserId)
activate repo
repo -->> auth: target identity
deactivate repo
note over auth,repo
An unknown system or missing user throws a 404 DomainException.
The attempt skips the remaining status and decision reads.
end note
auth -->> auth: unavailable reason or null
deactivate auth
alt target available
auth -> auth: 12. stableEffective(targetUserId, system)
activate auth
auth -->> auth: effective permissions
deactivate auth
alt UI
note over auth
Decide with Effective.has(identifier, UI).
end note
else API
auth -> auth: 13. stableApi(targetUserId, system, identifier)
activate auth
auth -->> auth: allowed
deactivate auth
end
else target user or system disabled
note over auth
Use empty effective permissions and allowed=false.
end note
end
end
alt attempt completed
auth -> repo: 14. version()
activate repo
repo -->> auth: current version
deactivate repo
note over auth,repo
If the version matches, finish with SimulationResult.
Otherwise repeat the whole attempt.
end note
else DomainException caught during lookup or decision
opt status below 500
auth -> repo: 15. version()
activate repo
repo -->> auth: current version
deactivate repo
end
break status at least 500 or version unchanged
auth -->> obj: DomainException with original status and code
end
note over auth
A changed version on a client error retries the whole attempt.
end note
end
end
break three attempts exhausted
auth -->> obj: 503 AUTHORIZATION_UNSTABLE
end
auth -->> auth: SimulationResult
deactivate auth
auth -->> ctl: SimulationResult
deactivate auth
note over ctl
Return allowed, reason and traceId.
Reason is USER_DISABLED / SYSTEM_DISABLED, ALLOW or DENY.
end note
opt explain=true
ctl -> restType: 16. effective(decision.effective())
activate restType
restType -->> ctl: effective permissions
deactivate restType
note over ctl
Include the explanation trace and effective permissions.
end note
end
ctl -> restType: 17. ok(result)
activate restType
restType -->> ctl: response envelope
deactivate restType
ctl -->> ctl: response
deactivate ctl
ctl -->> obj: HTTP 200 with simulation response
deactivate ctl
deactivate obj
@enduml